 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia place of death Basford 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia languages spoken , written or signed English 0 references occupation association football player 0 references association football manager 1 reference Soccerbase manager ID 599 stated in Soccerbase.com retrieved 7 April 2022 position played\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 13, \"text\": \"August 1939 .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 14, \"end\": 99, \"text\": \"He appeared for the club 345 times scoring 4 goals ; plus another 144 wartime games .\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 100, \"end\": 167, \"text\": \"He missed only 12 League games in seven seasons from 1947 to 1954 .\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 168, \"end\": 231, \"text\": \"He also sat on Aston Villa 's board of directors in the 1970s .\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 232, \"end\": 377, \"text\": \"He was in line for an England call-up in 1946 , but an injury meant he could not play , and he never got another chance to play for his country .\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 378, \"end\": 445, \"text\": \"His only honour with Villa was winning the League War Cup in 1944 .\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d02\", \"start\": 446, \"end\": 478, \"text\": \"Post-football career [ edit ] He\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0089-e23ee3cabda8:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Harry Parkes\", \"scope\": \"footballer\", \"claim\": \"Harold Arnold \\\"Harry\\\" Parkes was born in S